# ReBSD PCC Port TODO

Status: active
Scope: maintain the imported Portable C Compiler as a supported opt-in
ReBSD/MIPS C userland compiler while keeping the default GCC-based kernel and
userland build unchanged.  TLS/shared libraries and `p++`/C++ are future work,
not active items for the current C/static-a.out PCC milestone.

## Ground Rules

- Kernel builds stay on the existing GCC flow for now.
- Userland builds default to GCC.
- `MIPS_ROOTFS_COMPILER=pcc` and `N64_USERLAND_COMPILER=pcc` are supported
  opt-in C userland modes after the Malta, Malta64/R4000, and real N64 gates.
- ReBSD must keep using its existing `as`, `ld`, `ar`, and `ranlib`; no GNU
  binutils or LLVM dependency is allowed for the target toolchain.
- First working target is big-endian MIPS o32 for Malta and N64/VR4300-class
  hardware.
- PCC may expose ReBSD macros, but it must keep RetroBSD compatibility macros
  while the tree and ports still expect them.

