## Future Work, Not Current PCC Milestone

- [ ] TLS support.
  - The current ReBSD/MIPS PCC target is static a.out and deliberately rejects
    thread-local storage.
  - Keep TLS-only upstream tests as expected-fail policy cases until ReBSD has
    a concrete TLS ABI and runtime plan.
- [ ] Shared libraries/PIC support.
  - The current target has no `-shared`, runtime shared object loader, `rpath`,
    or shared-library ABI.
  - Keep shared-library/PIC upstream tests as expected-fail policy cases until
    ReBSD has a concrete shared-library ABI and loader plan.
- [ ] `p++`/C++ frontend and runtime.
  - Do not publish `/usr/bin/p++` or `/usr/libexec/pcc/cxxcom` in default
    rootfs images for now.
  - Revisit only as a separate C++ phase with frontend coverage, target
    compile/link/run gates, and a ctor/dtor startup policy.
- [ ] Optimize hot MIPS `libpcc.a` helpers in assembly.
  - The current canonical helper implementations are C, which keeps the
    correctness work auditable while Malta64 and N64 validation are still
    being hardened.
  - After the C helper set stays stable, add MIPS assembly implementations for
    selected hot 64-bit arithmetic, shift, and conversion helpers and keep the
    C versions as the reference oracle/fallback.

