- [ ] Add a compact late MIPS peephole/scheduling pass.
  - Use a short instruction window, initially 3-5 instructions, after final
    instruction selection.
  - Fill branch delay slots with safe independent work such as address updates,
    loop counter updates, invariant moves, or stores whose ordering is known
    safe.
  - Separate load-use and dependent FP operations when an independent
    instruction is available; otherwise leave a real `nop`.
  - Prefer refusing uncertain transformations over creating backend-specific
    correctness risk.
- [ ] Reduce avoidable frame-pointer and outgoing-argument stack traffic.
  - Rework MIPS call lowering so fixed outgoing argument area handling does not
    force `$fp` in ordinary non-variable-frame functions.
  - Preserve the existing o32 ABI fixes for struct returns, stack-passed
    64-bit arguments, varargs, and aggregate arguments.
  - Measure spills and load/store counts before and after; do not mix this
    with scheduler patches.
- [ ] Tune hard-float codegen for VR4300.
  - Replace unconditional FPU memory-operation `nop` padding with dependency
    scheduling.
  - Keep helper calls only where they preserve required IEEE/NaN behavior; do
    not replace correctness-sensitive helper paths with raw FPU instructions
    unless the existing N64/Malta tests prove equivalence.

