Success criteria:

- [ ] Short term: reduce PCC Linpack `nop` count and text size materially while
  keeping all PCC correctness gates green.
- [ ] Medium term: reach roughly 75-85% of GCC performance on real N64 with
  backend-only and ABI/scheduler work.
- [ ] Stretch target: reach 90-100% of GCC on representative workloads after
  adding small target-independent inlining/specialization and strength
  reduction, without making MIPS backend maintenance substantially harder.

